{
  "note": "Tokens declared somewhere the scope that needs them cannot reach. FREEZE: a `:root` declaration that reads a re-scopable seed substitutes once on <html>, so a scope below it inherits the answer root gave \u2014 the cure is `--x: initial` with the formula at the call site (docs/TOKENS.md). REACH: a bare `var(--t)` on an element where --t computes to nothing, because --t is declared only under a selector that element is not inside. Every entry is DEBT and the list may only SHRINK; the gate fails on anything new. Keyed on the ARRANGEMENT and never on a frame, an element or a measured value \u2014 a pixel in the key makes every known entry read as new on a different renderer (preview/frame-overflow.baseline.json learned that the hard way). `seenOn` is where to go and look.",
  "tracked": "gh#834 + gh#835 opened this list. Both are FIXED and neither is in it. gh#848 retired two more (--segmented-track-background, --segmented-item-selected-background: `initial` with their formulas at the call site; measured in Chromium with `.dark` on a <div> rather than <html>, the track went rgb(244,243,240) -> rgb(49,47,43)).\n  WHY THIS LIST GREW 67 -> 88, WHICH IT IS NOT ALLOWED TO DO (gh#854). The 21 additions are not new defects and not a regression: the GATE widened. COLOUR_SEEDS was a hand-kept array of 18 names and the dark theme block re-declares 36, so everything bound to --muted-foreground, --secondary, --secondary-foreground, --popover-foreground or --warning was filtered out by the tier clause and had never reached this file. Those tokens were frozen the whole time; only the instrument was blind. The seeds are now DERIVED from foundation.css's dark block, so a role added there seeds this gate for free \u2014 the same move regen-generated.mjs makes for generators, and for the same reason: the header of check-frame-token-scope.mjs already recorded that a hand-kept list is how the --font-size-* ramp went unseen for three releases.\n  AND THE RULE IS NOW ENFORCED. `--update-baseline` used to rewrite this file unconditionally while the note above claimed the list may only SHRINK \u2014 a rule in prose and not in code, which would have absorbed a real regression without a word. It now refuses to grow unless `--accept-growth` is passed, and that flag is for exactly one situation: you widened the gate, and you say so here.\n  WHAT IS LEFT, AND WHAT IT IS. Every remaining FREEZE entry is a `:root` declaration that reads a seed docs/CUSTOMER-THEMING.md tells a consumer they may re-scope, so a [data-tenant] or .dark subtree that sets that seed will NOT move the knob. The colour half is the gh#687 shape and is the dangerous half (a frozen light surface under dark ink). The --radius-* and --shadow-* families are the same defect one tier over and are the obvious next tranche.\n  NOT IN THIS LIST, ON PURPOSE: the ~230 component tokens that mirror a foundation step at :root (`--badge-font-size: var(--font-size-xs)`). They are frozen too, and they are the third tranche; see the tier clause in scripts/check-frame-token-scope.mjs for the measurement that kept them out of the gate rather than out of the truth.",
  "count": 88,
