  "intentional": {
    "REACH \u00b7 backdrop-filter \u00b7 --topbar-backdrop-blur-size \u00b7 .ui-topbar": "gh#831 \u2014 the glass bar is OPT-IN and expresses its OFF state as an empty knob. `--topbar-backdrop-blur-size: initial` at :root, read BARE so `blur()` has nothing to substitute, the declaration is invalid at computed-value time, and the bar blurs nothing. A fallback here would make the glass the default. src/styles/__tests__/topbar-glass.test.ts asserts the absence of the fallback, so the two guards agree.",
    "REACH \u00b7 background-color \u00b7 --topbar-background-alpha \u00b7 .ui-topbar": "gh#831 \u2014 the other half of the same opt-in. `hsl(var(--background) / var(--topbar-background-alpha))` with the alpha empty is invalid, so the bar paints no fill at all, which is the documented default. Setting the knob (e.g. 85%) is what turns the glass on."
  },
